{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "Gating a short path against a long path does not necessarily remove stale context: deeper block inputs and residual connections already contain distant history. The proposed mechanism needs evidence beyond gate values.",
    "The architecture lacks exact short-path dilations, kernel sizes, normalization placement, intermediate padding masks, gate initialization and residual equations. A positive gate bias favors the short path in the supplied equation, so baseline-preserving initialization requires a negative bias.",
    "Adding a convolution branch increases capacity and computation. Without a fixed-gate control using the same branches, improvements cannot be attributed specifically to adaptive context selection.",
    "No baseline validation HR@10, validation schedule, checkpoint-selection rule or GPU-budget allocation is reported. Selection over only 200 validation users per category also risks validation overfitting.",
    "Originality and implementation-difficulty scores are provisional without closer comparison to gated causal convolution methods or measured runtime. Sampled margins and simulator feedback do not establish stale context as the cause of ranking errors."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify whether the gate can suppress distant information and identify reproducible implementation details and closer prior art.",
      "query": "In NextItNet and gated causal temporal convolution networks, how do residual connections and stacked receptive fields affect a gate mixing short- and long-dilation branches? Find explicit block equations, causal normalization and padding practices, and initialization methods that preserve the original residual block."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Distinguish adaptive context selection from extra capacity and assess whether another small NextItNet modification deserves priority.",
      "query": "What controlled ablations in NextItNet or convolutional sequential recommendation distinguish benefits of content-dependent dilation gates from additional parameters, fixed multiscale branches, and shorter history windows? Include evidence about stale-context sensitivity, accuracy, and training cost without pretrained models."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Define a credible validation and selection plan under the fixed benchmark and limited search budget.",
      "query": "For sequential recommendation evaluated with HR@10 using one positive and 99 sampled negatives for 200 fixed validation users per dataset, what methods quantify paired ranking uncertainty and reduce repeated-validation selection bias? Consider four-dataset macro averaging, fixed training seed, checkpoint selection, and a fixed GPU search budget without test access."
    }
  ]
}
